e5": "V3: Ctrl+C key emit to the speech cancel at the server (the L2 path), then the app stops the flood and prints ^C and the prompt; v3_stale counts flood lines spoken after the key", "note6": "probe #11 (type; before: type \"V\", type \"y\") wanted \"3\", heard [-45.1ms \"V\", -23.5ms \"y\", +0.3ms \"3\", +58.2ms \"Sorry, try again.\\n[sudo] password for me:\"]", "note7": "VR: numpad review of a held terminal screen; vr_ipc_calls are application calls during the series (gate 0)", "note8": "VF: a pager page, a cursor row moved by Down, an htop-style repaint, an edit on a full screen, a 60x200 screen in ASCII and Cyrillic (caret mid-screen, Left)", "note9": "VB: a second terminal floods at 60 frames/s while the focused one is typed in; the key echo and the shell echo of the focused one are the only speech", "note10": "VW: output after Alt+Tab into the terminal before any key; lost per case [0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0] (order, FOCUSED lag, bounce: [(\"activate_first\", 0, false), (\"focus_first\", 0, false), (\"focus_first\", 8, false), (\"activate_first\", 8, false), (\"focus_first\", 8, true), (\"focus_first\", 160, false), (\"focus_first\", 400, false)]); latency is frame emit to SPEAK as in V1"},
